IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III, regs 68 to 76: the application for a reduction of the
-- employer's premium rate, the categories of insured persons, the effective date, the officer's decisions, the
-- employer's notices, the appeal and the transitional provision. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4.
-- Unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATIONS. The employer applies and must give notices; the Commission (an officer) decides, must hear the
-- employer in one case, and may reconsider. The insured persons are affected through the category they are placed in
-- (reg 69(1)) and the date from which the reduction applies (reg 71). A duty with a deadline is encoded as the last
-- day plus a rule that says whether the act was done in time: constitutive BOOLEANs, which can be asserted, not
-- regulative rules, whose traces `check.sh` does not count. A duty with no stated time ("immediately") takes a BOOLEAN
-- input for whether it was done immediately (fork F14).
-- Time limits are counted by the core's `the last day of n days after d` (the keel's fork F4: the last day counts).

§ `Regulation 68 -- the application`

§§ `Regulation 68(1) -- what the application must contain`

-- src:1127 | 68 (1) An application for a reduction of the employer’s premium rate in respect of insured persons, or for the continuation of such a reduction after the modification or replacement of a plan, shall be made to the Commission by the employer and shall
-- src:1128 | (a) be accompanied by a copy of the documents that represent the formal commitment referred to in subsection 67(1) or, if the application is for the continuation of a reduction, by a copy of the documents that have been modified or replaced;
-- src:1129 | (b) provide all the information necessary to determine whether the plan meets or continues to meet the requirements of this Part; and
-- src:1130 | (c) be accompanied by the employer's undertaking that the insured persons will benefit from the reduction of the employer's premium in an amount at least equal to five twelfths of the reduction, as required by subsection 69(1) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 68(1) (src:1127-1130)
GIVEN `the application is made to the Commission by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by a copy of the documents that represent the formal commitment referred to in subsection 67(1), or for a continuation the documents modified or replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides all the information necessary to determine whether the plan meets or continues to meet the requirements of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by the employer's undertaking that the insured persons will benefit from the reduction in an amount at least equal to five twelfths of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(1) the application is in the form the subsection requires` IF
        `the application is made to the Commission by the employer`
    AND `it is accompanied by a copy of the documents that represent the formal commitment referred to in subsection 67(1), or for a continuation the documents modified or replaced`
    AND `it provides all the information necessary to determine whether the plan meets or continues to meet the requirements of this Part`
    AND `it is accompanied by the employer's undertaking that the insured persons will benefit from the reduction in an amount at least equal to five twelfths of it`

§§ `Regulation 68(2) -- incomplete applications`

-- src:1131 | (2) Where an application referred to in subsection (1) is incomplete or where the Commission requires further information or documentation in order to make a decision on the application and the Commission requests that information or documentation from the employer, the employer shall provide the information or documentation within 30 days after the request is made, and where the information or documentation is not provided to the Commission within that time, an officer of the Commission shall make a decision on the existing information or documentation.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 68(2) (src:1131)
GIVEN `the day the Commission requests the information or documentation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 68(2) the last day for the employer to provide the information or documentation` MEANS
    `the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day the Commission requests the information or documentation`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 68(2) (src:1131)
GIVEN `the day the Commission requests the information or documentation` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer provides it, if the employer has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(2) the employer provided the information or documentation within 30 days after the request` IF
    CONSIDER `the day the employer provides it, if the employer has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST provided THEN provided AT MOST `reg 68(2) the last day for the employer to provide the information or documentation` `the day the Commission requests the information or documentation`

-- The officer decides "on the existing information or documentation" when the application is incomplete or the Commission
-- requires more, the Commission has asked the employer for it, and it is not provided in the 30 days.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 68(2) (src:1131)
GIVEN `the application is incomplete or the Commission requires further information or documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has requested it from the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer provided it within 30 days after the request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 68(2) an officer of the Commission is to make a decision on the existing information or documentation` IF
        `the application is incomplete or the Commission requires further information or documentation`
    AND `the Commission has requested it from the employer`
    AND (NOT `the employer provided it within 30 days after the request`)

§ `Regulation 69 -- categories, account numbers and remittances`

§§ `Regulation 69(1) -- the five categories`

-- src:1132 | 69 (1) In the case of an application for a reduction of the employer’s premium rate, or for the continuation of such a reduction, an employer shall group the insured persons employed by the employer into the following categories:
-- src:1133 | (a) insured persons who are covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 63;
-- src:1134 | (b) insured persons who are covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 64;
-- src:1135 | (c) insured persons who are covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 65, except the insured persons referred to in paragraph 65(d);
-- src:1136 | (d) insured persons who are covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 66, except the insured persons referred to in paragraph 65(d); and
-- src:1137 | (e) all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(1) (src:1132-1137)
DECLARE `er4 Category of insured persons` IS ONE OF
    `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 63`                                              -- (a)
    `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 64`                                              -- (b)
    `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 65, except those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`   -- (c)
    `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 66, except those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`   -- (d)
    `er4 all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`                                                    -- (e)

-- "Referred to in paragraph 65(d)": the insured persons whose eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred (as a
-- temporary or probationary employee). A plan of none of the four kinds, or one that does not satisfy its section,
-- puts the person among "all other insured persons".
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(1) (src:1132-1137)
GIVEN kind IS A `er4 Kind of wage-loss plan`
      `the plan satisfies the requirements of the section for its kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person's eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred as paragraph 65(d) contemplates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er4 Category of insured persons`
`reg 69(1) the category the insured person is placed in` MEANS
    IF NOT `the plan satisfies the requirements of the section for its kind`
    THEN `er4 all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `er4 a Weekly Indemnity Plan` THEN `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 63`
         WHEN `er4 a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` THEN `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 64`
         WHEN `er4 a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` THEN
             IF `the insured person's eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred as paragraph 65(d) contemplates`
             THEN `er4 all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`
             ELSE `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 65, except those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`
         WHEN `er4 an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` THEN
             IF `the insured person's eligibility to use paid sick leave is deferred as paragraph 65(d) contemplates`
             THEN `er4 all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`
             ELSE `er4 insured persons covered by a plan that satisfies the requirements of section 66, except those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`
         OTHERWISE `er4 all other insured persons, including those referred to in paragraph 65(d)`

§§ `Regulation 69(2) -- on an application for a reduction`

-- The employer's duty arises "on notification by the Commission that a plan satisfies the requirements"; once it has
-- arisen the employer must request a separate account number for each category immediately and notify the Commission
-- immediately on receipt. Before the notification there is nothing to comply with.
-- src:1138 | (2) In the case of an application for a reduction, the employer shall
-- src:1139 | (a) on notification by the Commission that a plan satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66, request immediately from the Canada Revenue Agency a separate account number for each category of insured persons who are covered by a plan that entitles the employer to a reduction; and
-- src:1140 | (b) notify the Commission immediately on receipt of those account numbers.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(2) (src:1138-1140)
GIVEN `the Commission has notified the employer that a plan satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer immediately requested from the Canada Revenue Agency a separate account number for each category of insured persons covered by a plan that entitles the employer to a reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer immediately notified the Commission on receipt of those account numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(2) the employer has done what the subsection requires` IF
        (NOT `the Commission has notified the employer that a plan satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`)
    OR  (    `the employer immediately requested from the Canada Revenue Agency a separate account number for each category of insured persons covered by a plan that entitles the employer to a reduction`
         AND `the employer immediately notified the Commission on receipt of those account numbers`)

§§ `Regulation 69(3) -- on a change in the categories`

-- src:1141 | (3) If a modification or replacement of a plan results in a change to the previously established categories of insured persons, the employer shall
-- src:1142 | (a) on notification by the Commission that the plan as modified or replaced satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66, request immediately from the Canada Revenue Agency a new account number for any newly established category; and
-- src:1143 | (b) notify the Commission immediately on receipt of that account number.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(3) (src:1141-1143)
GIVEN `a modification or replacement of the plan results in a change to the previously established categories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has notified the employer that the plan as modified or replaced satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer immediately requested from the Canada Revenue Agency a new account number for any newly established category` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer immediately notified the Commission on receipt of that account number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(3) the employer has done what the subsection requires` IF
        (NOT (    `a modification or replacement of the plan results in a change to the previously established categories`
              AND `the Commission has notified the employer that the plan as modified or replaced satisfies the requirements of section 63, 64, 65 or 66`))
    OR  (    `the employer immediately requested from the Canada Revenue Agency a new account number for any newly established category`
         AND `the employer immediately notified the Commission on receipt of that account number`)

§§ `Regulation 69(4) -- remittances and information returns for each year of a reduction`

-- src:1144 | (4) For each year for which a reduction of the employer’s premium rate is applicable, the employer shall
-- src:1145 | (a) beginning not later than the first remittance for the first month from which the employer’s reduction is applicable, remit to the Canada Revenue Agency the employer’s premium payable in respect of all insured persons in each category for which an account number has been received; and
-- src:1146 | (b) submit to the Canada Revenue Agency, for each account number, an information return that shows the total amount of insurable earnings, of employees’ premiums and of employer’s premiums in respect of all insured persons in the category for which the account number was issued.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 69(4) (src:1144-1146)
GIVEN `the employer remitted to the Canada Revenue Agency the employer's premium payable in respect of all insured persons in each category for which an account number has been received, beginning not later than the first remittance for the first month from which the reduction is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer submitted to the Canada Revenue Agency, for each account number, an information return showing the total insurable earnings, employees' premiums and employer's premiums of all insured persons in the category` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 69(4) the employer has done what the subsection requires for the year` IF
        `the employer remitted to the Canada Revenue Agency the employer's premium payable in respect of all insured persons in each category for which an account number has been received, beginning not later than the first remittance for the first month from which the reduction is applicable`
    AND `the employer submitted to the Canada Revenue Agency, for each account number, an information return showing the total insurable earnings, employees' premiums and employer's premiums of all insured persons in the category`

§ `Regulation 70 -- the plan is modified or replaced`

-- src:1147 | 70 If the plan on which a reduction of the employer’s premium rate is based is modified or replaced, the employer shall
-- src:1148 | (a) notify the Commission within 30 days after the modification or replacement; and
-- src:1149 | (b) apply for a continuation of the reduction in accordance with section 68.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 70(a) (src:1147-1148)
GIVEN `the day the plan is modified or replaced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 70(a) the last day for the employer to notify the Commission` MEANS
    `the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day the plan is modified or replaced`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 70(a) (src:1147-1148)
GIVEN `the day the plan is modified or replaced` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer notifies the Commission, if the employer has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70(a) the employer notified the Commission within 30 days after the modification or replacement` IF
    CONSIDER `the day the employer notifies the Commission, if the employer has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST notified THEN notified AT MOST `reg 70(a) the last day for the employer to notify the Commission` `the day the plan is modified or replaced`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 70 (src:1147-1149)
GIVEN `the employer notified the Commission within 30 days after the modification or replacement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer applied for a continuation of the reduction in accordance with section 68` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 70 the employer has done what the section requires` IF
        `the employer notified the Commission within 30 days after the modification or replacement`
    AND `the employer applied for a continuation of the reduction in accordance with section 68`

§ `Regulation 71 -- the effective date of the reduction`

-- Initial application: made on or before the 15th, the first day of the following month; after the 15th, the first
-- day of the second following month. Continuation: the effective date of the modification or replacement.
-- (This is not reg 67(4), which dates the day a plan becomes or ceases to be a qualifying plan.)
-- src:1150 | 71 The effective date of a reduction of the employer’s premium rate under subsection 62(1) is,
-- src:1151 | (a) in the case of an initial application for a reduction,
-- src:1152 | (i) the first day of the month following the month in which the application was made, if it was made on or before the 15th day of the month, or
-- src:1153 | (ii) the first day of the second month following the month in which the application was made, if it was made after the 15th day of the month, and
-- src:1154 | (b) in the case of an application for the continuation of a reduction, the effective date of the modification or replacement of the plan.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 71 (src:1150-1154)
GIVEN `the application is an initial application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the effective date of the modification or replacement of the plan` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 71 the effective date of the reduction of the employer's premium rate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the application is an initial application`
                THEN `the effective date of the modification or replacement of the plan`
           IF DATE_DAY `the day the application was made` AT MOST 15
                THEN `add months` (YearMonthDay (DATE_YEAR `the day the application was made`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the application was made`) 1) 1
           OTHERWISE `add months` (YearMonthDay (DATE_YEAR `the day the application was made`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the application was made`) 1) 2

§ `Regulation 72 -- the officer's decisions`

-- src:1155 | 72 (1) On receiving an application that is in accordance with section 68, an officer of the Commission shall decide whether the employer meets or continues to meet the requirements for receiving a reduction under this Part and shall notify the employer of the decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 72(1) (src:1155)
GIVEN `an application in accordance with section 68 has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(1) an officer of the Commission is to decide whether the employer meets or continues to meet the requirements and notify the employer` IF
    `an application in accordance with section 68 has been received`

-- src:1156 | (2) If an employer does not comply with section 70, an officer of the Commission shall, after learning of the non-compliance and giving the employer an opportunity to be heard, make the decision referred to in subsection (1) and notify the employer of the decision.
-- The officer must first learn of the non-compliance and give the employer an opportunity to be heard.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 72(2) (src:1156)
GIVEN `the employer does not comply with section 70` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has learned of the non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(2) an officer of the Commission is to give the employer an opportunity to be heard, then decide and notify the employer` IF
        `the employer does not comply with section 70`
    AND `the officer has learned of the non-compliance`

-- src:1157 | (3) If an employer’s plan ceases to meet the requirements of paragraph 63(d), an officer of the Commission shall terminate entitlement to the reduction and notify the employer of the decision.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 72(3) (src:1157)
GIVEN `the plan met the requirements of paragraph 63(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan now meets the requirements of paragraph 63(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 72(3) an officer of the Commission is to terminate entitlement to the reduction and notify the employer` IF
        `the plan met the requirements of paragraph 63(d)`
    AND (NOT `the plan now meets the requirements of paragraph 63(d)`)

§ `Regulation 73 -- evidence on a late application`

-- src:1158 | 73 An employer who makes an application referred to in subsection 69(4) of the Act shall produce evidence that a qualifying plan pursuant to paragraph 67(3) was in effect during the period in respect of which the application is made.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 73 (src:1158)
GIVEN `the application is one referred to in subsection 69(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has produced evidence that a qualifying plan pursuant to paragraph 67(3) was in effect during the period in respect of which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 73 the employer has produced the evidence the regulation requires` IF
        (NOT `the application is one referred to in subsection 69(4) of the Act`)
    OR  `the employer has produced evidence that a qualifying plan pursuant to paragraph 67(3) was in effect during the period in respect of which the application is made`

§ `Regulation 74 -- termination of the plan`

-- src:1161 | 74 An employer shall, within 30 days after termination of a plan on which a reduction of the employer’s premium rate is based, notify the Commission of the plan’s termination.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 74 (src:1161)
GIVEN `the day the plan is terminated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 74 the last day for the employer to notify the Commission of the termination` MEANS
    `the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day the plan is terminated`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 74 (src:1161)
GIVEN `the day the plan is terminated` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer notifies the Commission, if the employer has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 74 the employer notified the Commission of the termination within 30 days` IF
    CONSIDER `the day the employer notifies the Commission, if the employer has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST notified THEN notified AT MOST `reg 74 the last day for the employer to notify the Commission of the termination` `the day the plan is terminated`

§ `Regulation 75 -- appeal to the Commission`

-- The employer may appeal "within one year after the day on which notice of the decision or new decision is sent":
-- the last day is the same date a year later (`add years` clamps 29 February). The three decisions named are a decision
-- under reg 72, under Act s 69(4) (late applications) and a new decision under Act s 69(5) (reconsideration); for any
-- other decision the regulation says nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:1164 | 75 An employer may appeal to the Commission a decision made pursuant to section 72 of these Regulations or pursuant to subsection 69(4) of the Act or a new decision made pursuant to subsection 69(5) of the Act, within one year after the day on which notice of the decision or new decision is sent to the employer.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 75 (src:1164)
DECLARE `er4 Decision the employer may appeal to the Commission` IS ONE OF
    `er4 a decision made pursuant to section 72 of these Regulations`
    `er4 a decision made pursuant to subsection 69(4) of the Act`
    `er4 a new decision made pursuant to subsection 69(5) of the Act`
    `er4 another decision`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 75 (src:1164)
GIVEN `the day notice of the decision is sent to the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 75 the last day for the employer to appeal` MEANS
    `add years` `the day notice of the decision is sent to the employer` 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 75 (src:1164)
GIVEN decision IS A `er4 Decision the employer may appeal to the Commission`
      `the day notice of the decision is sent to the employer` IS A DATE
      `the day the employer appeals` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 75 the employer may appeal to the Commission` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision
    WHEN `er4 another decision` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (`the day the employer appeals` AT MOST `reg 75 the last day for the employer to appeal` `the day notice of the decision is sent to the employer`)

§ `Regulation 76 -- the premium for 1995`

-- src:1167 | 76 The Commission may reconsider an application by an employer for a reduction of the employer's premium for the year 1995 where the employer
-- src:1168 | (a) has made the application before December 4, 1994;
-- src:1169 | (b) has been considered for a premium reduction for the year 1995; and
-- src:1170 | (c) would have been entitled to a greater premium reduction if the application had been made on or after December 4, 1994.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76 (src:1167-1170)
`reg 76 December 4, 1994` MEANS YearMonthDay 1994 12 4

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76 (src:1167-1170)
GIVEN `the day the employer made the application for the year 1995` IS A DATE
      `the employer has been considered for a premium reduction for the year 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer would have been entitled to a greater premium reduction if the application had been made on or after December 4, 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76 the Commission may reconsider the application for the year 1995` IF
        `the day the employer made the application for the year 1995` LESS THAN `reg 76 December 4, 1994`
    AND `the employer has been considered for a premium reduction for the year 1995`
    AND `the employer would have been entitled to a greater premium reduction if the application had been made on or after December 4, 1994`
